# ── Confidential / real business data — NEVER commit ──────────────────────────
# Real company data (financials, Fulfil exports, executive reports) must never be
# committed or pushed. See .claude/rules/no-pii.md, .claude/rules/security-secrets.md,
# and docs/adr/0003. Keep real samples in data/samples/ LOCAL ONLY; commit only
# synthetic, clearly-fake fixtures.
data/samples/*.xlsx
data/samples/*.xls
data/samples/*.xlsm
data/samples/*.csv
data/samples/*.parquet

# ── Generated report output — local only, never commit ────────────────────────
# Bob writes the finished WAR workbook here (see plans/PRD-WAR-Automation.md).
# Real financials — keep out of git.
output/*
!output/README.md

# ── Secrets / credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# Exception: the placeholder-only template IS committed (BD-003). Real .env* stay ignored above.
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
**/secrets/*
**/credentials*

# ── Local tooling / MCP config — never commit ─────────────────────────────────
# .mcp.json wires up local MCP servers (e.g. Trello). Connecting an external
# service is a per-developer, human-gated choice (see .claude/rules/external-services.md)
# and the file may later hold endpoints/tokens — keep it local only.
.mcp.json

# ── Python artifacts (v1 stack — docs/adr/0002) ───────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Packaging outputs from `pip install -e .` / builds (BD-001)
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
